From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:42:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1775/3799] soh: rename func_800BB03C ->
 DbCamera_PlayCurrentCut

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: the one-argument entry point that plays the current cut on the global debug camera.
Defined in soh/src/code/db_camera.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/db_camera.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/db_camera.c b/soh/src/code/db_camera.c
index 5e104c86e..a42aac4f1 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/db_camera.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/db_camera.c
@@ -2264,7 +2264,8 @@ s32 DbCamera_UpdateDemoControl(DbCamera* dbCamera, Camera* cam) {
     return 1;
 }
 
-void func_800BB03C(Camera* cam) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_800BB03C: the one-argument entry point that plays the current cut on the global debug camera.
+void DbCamera_PlayCurrentCut(Camera* cam) {
     DbCamera_PlayCut(cam, sDbCamPtr);  // was func_800B91B0 [LLM:HIGH]
 }
 
